during the interval between F2 and F3, the northern sunspot group with relatively compact configuration undergoes

rapid expansion, which resulted in its fragmentation into three distinct parts (indicated by arrows in Figure 9(j)). The

magnetogram images cotemporal with the continuum observations are shown in Figures 9(k)–(m). The eastern and

western PILs are indicated by red and sky-blue dotted lines, respectively in Figure 9(k). We observe clear features

of flux cancellation and emergence. The sky-blue arrows indicate a substantial cancellation of negative flux near the



