5. MORPHOLOGY AND EVOLUTION OF PHOTOSPHERIC LONGITUDINAL CURRENTS

We show the morphological changes associated with the photospheric longitudinal current in response to the magnetic

field changes in Figure 11. On the photosphere, the vertical component of the electric current density (i.e., Jz) can be

obtained from the horizontal magnetic field components (i.e., Bx and By) using the Ampere’s law (Kontogiannis et al.

2017; Fleishman & Pevtsov 2018; Fursyak et al. 2020):

Jz =
