The magnetic field components (Bz, -By, Bx) in Heliographic Cartesian Coordinate can be approximately obtained

from the corresponding field components (Br, Bθ, Bφ) in the Heliocentric Spherical Coordinate (Gary & Hagyard 1990).

In order to calculate the longitudinal current (Iz) from longitudinal current density (Jz), we need to multiply Jz with

the area of one pixel, i.e., 13.14×1010 m2. In Figure 11, we present the distribution of current (i.e., Iz) along with the

structure of the radial component of magnetic field (i.e., Br) within the flaring region before the start of the flares.

The top, middle, and bottom panels of Figure 11 correspond to F1, F2, and F3, respectively. For better visualization,

we saturate the current values at ±0.5×1010 A in all the panels. The color code for all the Iz-maps (Figures 11(a),

(c), and (e)) is shown by a colorbar in Figure 11(a). We observe significant amount of current concentration along the



